{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1194 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "fda62f4e8dfeebc15757e4571e83cc94452988ec2c059264ca38afdbe50a0f97" :edb/db-before-t 1193 :edb/db-after-t 1194 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534506 50 #inst "2026-10-07T18:44:04.327Z" 13194139534506 true] [17592186100806 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292422 13194139534506 true] [17592186100806 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292426 13194139534506 true] [17592186100807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292415 13194139534506 true] [17592186100807 1020 #edb/ref 17592186292429 13194139534506 true] [17592186101452 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(\\frac{1}{xy} + \\frac{1}{y})\\frac{dy}{dx} = 1$ that satisfies $y(1) = e$." 13194139534506 false] [17592186101452 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1$ that satisfies $y(1)=e.$" 13194139534506 true] [17592186101452 1145 "Combine the coefficient of $y'$:\n$$\\frac{x+1}{xy}y'=1,\\qquad \\frac{y'}y=\\frac{x}{x+1}=1-\\frac1{x+1}.$$\nNear the initial point $x=1$, integration gives $\\ln|y|=x-\\ln|x+1|+C$, hence $y=Ke^x/(x+1)$. Using $y(1)=e$ yields $e=Ke/2$, so $K=2$ and\n$$y=\\frac{2e^x}{x+1}.$$\nUse the interval $x>0$ containing the initial point; the original equation is undefined at $x=0$." 13194139534506 false] [17592186101452 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}(\\frac{1+x}{x})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x}{x+1} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{x}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int (1-\\frac{1}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|} & ={e}^{x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{x-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|+C} \\\\ |y| & ={e}^{x}\\cdot {e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|}\\cdot {e}^{C} \\\\ y & =\\frac{K{e}^{x}}{x+1},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=e$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =e \\\\ \\frac{K{e}^{1}}{1+1} & =e \\\\ K & =2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $(\\frac{1}{xy}+\\frac{1}{y})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=1$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=e$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{2{e}^{x}}{x+1}\\,.\n$$" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292415 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292416 13194139534506 true] [17592186292415 1089 "q-104059" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292415 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534506 true] [17592186292415 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies $y(-1)=1.$" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292415 1113 #uuid "919dc14f-ff69-5952-b9d3-1351ffc6437d" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292415 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & =-\\frac{1}{x}+x+C \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =\\frac{1-{x}^{2}-Cx}{x} \\\\ y & =\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{2}-Cx}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{x}{1-{x}^{2}-Cx},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(-1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(-1) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{-1}{1-(-1)^{2}-C(-1)} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{-1}{C} & =1 \\\\ C & =-1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+{y}^{2}$ that satisfies the condition $y(-1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}\\,.\n$$" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292417 13194139534506 true] [17592186292416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292418 13194139534506 true] [17592186292416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292419 13194139534506 true] [17592186292416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292420 13194139534506 true] [17592186292416 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292421 13194139534506 true] [17592186292416 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534506 true] [17592186292416 1041 "selection" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292416 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292420 13194139534506 true] [17592186292416 1110 #uuid "42ce8856-c1f6-5ff7-bc9a-c230fc99d9dc" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292417 1034 "y=\\frac{x}{2x+{x}^{2}}" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292417 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534506 true] [17592186292417 1111 #uuid "d948bac9-62a7-5665-95df-522f8b717271" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292418 1034 "y=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}-2x}" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292418 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534506 true] [17592186292418 1111 #uuid "9a755514-92bb-506a-8775-2d1708304b32" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292419 1034 "y=-\\frac{x}{1+x+{x}^{2}}" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292419 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534506 true] [17592186292419 1111 #uuid "c027f59a-7575-5547-8e1a-bc2ccbcccf58" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292420 1034 "y=\\frac{x}{1+x-{x}^{2}}" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292420 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534506 true] [17592186292420 1111 #uuid "cf27878b-c87e-50bf-a22a-f8c50efcdbc7" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292421 1034 "y=\\frac{x}{2+2x-{x}^{2}}" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292421 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534506 true] [17592186292421 1111 #uuid "b5984bc1-4d99-5874-a48a-f57bbe65a914" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292422 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292423 13194139534506 true] [17592186292422 1089 "q-347853" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292422 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534506 true] [17592186292422 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2{y}^{2}=0$\nthat satisfies the condition $y(0)=2.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292422 1113 #uuid "2221490e-f21a-588c-b91a-30cee47bc521" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292422 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2{y}^{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =2x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2x+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\frac{1}{2x+C},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{1}{2(0)+C} \\\\ C & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\frac{2}{4x+1}.\n$$" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292423 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292424 13194139534506 true] [17592186292423 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292425 13194139534506 true] [17592186292423 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534506 true] [17592186292423 1041 "field-1" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292423 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292424 13194139534506 true] [17592186292423 1110 #uuid "6d39f3ea-9301-57f8-ab08-d613b890416e" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292424 1034 "\\frac{2}{4x+1}" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292424 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534506 true] [17592186292424 1111 #uuid "0a8eb70a-e41b-5bb2-8a1c-c2d892adb8b0" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292425 1034 "\\frac{2}{2x+1}" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292425 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534506 true] [17592186292425 1111 #uuid "782f563b-2517-5b65-b3d1-0639cd3da9d6" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292426 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292427 13194139534506 true] [17592186292426 1089 "q-355525" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292426 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534506 true] [17592186292426 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y){y}^{′}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)=0$ that satisfies $y(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=0.$ Assume that $-\\frac{\\pi }{6}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{6}.$\n\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292426 1113 #uuid "90c059c9-cfbc-5121-8811-b73c677022f4" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292426 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3{C}_{1}.$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(\\frac{\\pi }{8})=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{8}) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8})+C \\\\ 0 & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+C \\\\ 0 & =0+C \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292427 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292428 13194139534506 true] [17592186292427 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534506 true] [17592186292427 1041 "field-1" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292427 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292428 13194139534506 true] [17592186292427 1110 #uuid "9ecc2147-d9e9-5bbb-baa5-a19422b1e77b" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292428 1034 "-\\frac{3}{4}\\cos(4x)" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292428 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534506 true] [17592186292428 1111 #uuid "4103ec85-0df0-5ba8-8d38-0644036eed9f" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292429 1017 #edb/ref 17592186292430 13194139534506 true] [17592186292429 1089 "q-79425" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292429 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534506 true] [17592186292429 1100 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{y}^{3}=4x$ that satisfies $y(0)=1.$  Assume that $y>0.$" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292429 1113 #uuid "02d23995-f689-5881-b3ec-6224edc19266" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292429 1145 "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2x{y}^{3} & =4x \\\\ 3{y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x(2+{y}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}y & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo calculate the integral on the left-hand side of this equality, we use a substitution\n\n$$\nu=2+{y}^{3}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nThen  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{y}^{2}}{2+{y}^{3}}\\text{d}y & =\\int \\frac{1}{2+{y}^{3}}(3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|+{C}_{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})+{C}_{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $y>0.$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})+{C}_{2} & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3}) & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1}-{C}_{2} \\\\ {e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2+{y}^{3})} & ={e}^{{x}^{2}+{C}_{1}-{C}_{2}} \\\\ 2+{y}^{3} & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =K{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm {e}^{{C}_{1}-{C}_{2}}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=1$ to find $K:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{1}^{3} & =K{e}^{{0}^{2}}-2 \\\\ 1 & =K-2 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2.\n$$" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292430 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292431 13194139534506 true] [17592186292430 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292432 13194139534506 true] [17592186292430 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292433 13194139534506 true] [17592186292430 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292434 13194139534506 true] [17592186292430 1000 #edb/ref 17592186292435 13194139534506 true] [17592186292430 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534506 true] [17592186292430 1041 "selection" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292430 1104 #edb/ref 17592186292432 13194139534506 true] [17592186292430 1110 #uuid "cddc7849-107c-5824-b5d6-93695259dd65" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292431 1034 "{y}^{2}=3{e}^{x}-2" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292431 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534506 true] [17592186292431 1111 #uuid "89d02a14-92d3-5033-a057-9bd1ad6769e4" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292432 1034 "{y}^{3}=3{e}^{{x}^{2}}-2" 13194139534506 true] [17592186292432 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534